# Inputs that change the NATIVE (Rust / C++) engine build.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (audit 2026-09-18)
#   The cargo cache key used to hash the WHOLE versions.env. Because that file
#   also carries FUSION_VERSION, every release bump changed the key, forced a
#   full Rust rebuild, and — since Rust codegen is not bit-reproducible —
#   produced byte-level drift between otherwise identical builds. It was also
#   under-inclusive: a TEESIM_NDK_VERSION bump (declared in build.yml) did not
#   change the key at all, so stale Rust objects could be linked against a new
#   NDK, and patches were not covered either.
#
#   The key is now `cargo-<hash of this file + patches/teesim/**>-<NDK version>`,
#   i.e. exactly the inputs that can change the native build output. Bumping
#   FUSION_VERSION no longer triggers a Rust rebuild.
#
# MAINTENANCE
#   FINGERPRINT_REF here MUST equal TEESIM_REF in versions.env — the CI asserts this
#   before the cache step and fails the build on any mismatch, so a forgotten
#   edit can not silently serve a stale cache.
FINGERPRINT_REF=4f42350e8ad8d5f11111d2200f39d1d4d113a4df
